    {
      "text": "Cartier's Love bracelet needs a screwdriver.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook",
        "show": "bracelet",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Aldo Cipullo, an Italian designer, drew the Love bracelet in 1969.",
      "say": "Aldo Cipullo, an Italian designer, drew the Love bracelet in nineteen sixty-nine.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "workshop",
        "name": "Aldo Cipullo",
        "role": "Designer, 1969",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#4a3a5a",
            "hair": "curly",
            "hairColor": "#2e2420",
            "skin": "#f3d6bd",
            "expression": "focused",
            "facial": "mustache"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "He had worked at Tiffany and at David Webb before that.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Tiffany",
        "sub": "And David Webb",
        "color": "#4cc3a8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "His idea was to leave the screws showing,",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Visible screws",
        "sub": "The whole idea",
        "color": "#5bb4e8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "and lock them with a screwdriver that comes with the bracelet.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "bracelet",
        "label": "Comes with a screwdriver",
        "color": "#a98be0"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The screws were meant to stand for permanence.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "study",
        "name": "Aldo Cipullo",
        "role": "A symbol of permanence",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#4a3a5a",
            "hair": "curly",
            "hairColor": "#2e2420",
            "skin": "#f3d6bd",
            "expression": "worried"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Tiffany passed on the design, so he took it to Cartier.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Tiffany passed",
        "sub": "So he went to Cartier",
        "color": "#f0552e"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Cartier New York, then independent of Paris, backed it.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "vault",
        "name": "Michael Thomas",
        "role": "Head of Cartier New York",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#2a3a4a",
            "hair": "slick",
            "hairColor": "#6a5a4a",
            "skin": "#efc9a6",
            "expression": "proud"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#c8dc3c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It first sold for about $250.",
      "say": "It first sold for about two hundred fifty dollars.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "About $250",
        "sub": "The first price",
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Cartier gave it to couples like Elizabeth Taylor and Richard Burton.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Taylor and Burton",
        "sub": "Among the first couples",
        "color": "#a98be0"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The classic one takes someone else's help to close.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Two screws",
        "sub": "Someone else tightens them",
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "caption": "Aldo Cipullo designed the Cartier Love bracelet in 1969 with visible screws and a screwdriver that comes with it. Tiffany passed on the design, so he took it to Cartier New York, where it first sold for about $250.",
